nts", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 129478, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0175HvbrD7G7r9dcsBZrY8Aa", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 133265, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_014NAXtYq6k6pDm6QdWAbAgt", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate. The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging. checkout-api was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production (rollback approved). After the rollback, the service is healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions with a 0.2% error rate. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 171365, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014NAXtYq6k6pDm6QdWAbAgt", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 171365, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014NAXtYq6k6pDm6QdWAbAgt", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 175466, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again.\n\n- **What went wrong:** v2.3.1 was live in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. The rollback needed approval, which came through, and v2.3.0 is now running in all three regions.\n- **Check afterwards:** The service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure and the rollback, and notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014pSZ1K1Vs1aittndcqevux", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KNrHXhPzdYTJkqVw8ANHi3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018qxP5vXsJpsExdmUgjFk1d", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GMgDhEYH77XAbCwe8RbEMB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0175HvbrD7G7r9dcsBZrY8Aa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014NAXtYq6k6pDm6QdWAbAgt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate. The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging. checkout-api was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production (rollback approved). After the rollback, the service is healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions with a 0.2% error rate. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened a SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again.\n\n- **What went wrong:** v2.3.1 was live in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. The rollback needed approval, which came through, and v2.3.0 is now running in all three regions.\n- **Check afterwards:** The service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure and the rollback, and notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before it's deployed again.", "type": "text"}]}]}